## At work

While you wait for surgery, it may help to have:

- brighter task lighting, or a larger screen
- screen magnification software
- a change of duties if you drive for work and your sight is affected

Most people need a few days to a couple of weeks off after surgery, depending on their job. Avoid dusty or dirty work until your eye has healed.

## Is it a disability?

Cataracts are usually treated successfully, so most people are not covered by the Equality Act for long. If you have other conditions that affect your sight, you may be.

## Benefits

Cataracts alone do not usually qualify for PIP, because surgery works well for most people. If you have long-term sight loss from other conditions, read about [glaucoma](/conditions/brain-nerves-and-senses/glaucoma/) or [macular degeneration](/conditions/brain-nerves-and-senses/macular-degeneration/).

## Help with costs

You may be able to get help with the cost of sight tests and glasses. Try our [NHS health costs check](/support/health-costs/checker/).
